{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And Abraham gave all that he had to Isaac.</b> Wonder: how could he do so, as we say it is forbidden to transfer inheritance even from a bad son to a good one, for one does not know what seed will come from them, and it is written ״יכין צדיק [ורשע] ילבש״, and the world stands on the principle that our father Abraham upheld even eiruvei tavshilin. And one may answer that Abraham and Ishmael were converts, and we say that a convert does not inherit his fellow [convert father] — not by Torah law and not by rabbinic law. My master Samuel. And before the others were born, he had already given it to him, as it is written above: ״ויתן לו את כל אשר לו״."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The phrase 'וקי״ל בעלמא' is rendered as 'the world stands on the principle,' understanding קי״ל as a form of קיימא לן/קיימת לן; the exact Aramaic idiom here is slightly unusual and may reflect a textual variant."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:59.274020403Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}